2046
01:23:26,880 --> 01:23:29,880
Oh, no, I just lost a little weight, that's all.

2047
01:23:33,880 --> 01:23:37,880
Well, you look nice.

2048
01:23:37,880 --> 01:23:41,880
I've been thinking about it, and I think that we should get married.

2049
01:23:41,880 --> 01:23:43,880
Oh, Albie, come on.

2050
01:23:43,880 --> 01:23:46,880
What, you want to live out here or what do you think?

2051
01:23:46,880 --> 01:23:49,880
It's like living in munchkin land.

2052
01:23:49,880 --> 01:23:52,880
What do you mean? I mean, it's perfectly fine out here.

2053
01:23:52,880 --> 01:23:57,220
I mean, Tony's very nice, and, uh, well, I meet people,

2054
01:23:57,220 --> 01:23:59,520
and I go to parties, and we play tennis.

2055
01:23:59,520 --> 01:24:02,480
I mean, that's a very big step for me, you know?

2056
01:24:02,480 --> 01:24:06,220
I mean, I'm able to enjoy people more.

2057
01:24:06,220 --> 01:24:07,400
So what do you want?

2058
01:24:07,400 --> 01:24:09,020
You're not gonna come back to New York?

2059
01:24:09,020 --> 01:24:10,520
What's so great about New York?

2060
01:24:10,520 --> 01:24:11,640
I mean, it's a dying city.

2061
01:24:11,640 --> 01:24:13,560
You read Death in Venice.

2062
01:24:13,560 --> 01:24:14,940
Hey, you didn't read Death in Venice

2063
01:24:14,940 --> 01:24:16,279
till I bought it for you.

2064
01:24:16,279 --> 01:24:17,579
That's right, that's right.

2065
01:24:17,579 --> 01:24:20,000
You only gave me books with the word death in the title.

2066
01:24:20,000 --> 01:24:22,119
That's right, because it's an important issue.

2067
01:24:22,119 --> 01:24:25,119
Alvy, you're incapable of enjoying life, you know that?

2068
01:24:25,119 --> 01:24:27,119
I mean, you're like New York City.

2069
01:24:27,119 --> 01:24:30,119
You're just this person. You're like this island unto yourself.

2070
01:24:30,119 --> 01:24:33,119
I can't enjoy anything unless I... unless everybody is.

2071
01:24:33,119 --> 01:24:36,119
You know, if one guy is starving someplace, that's...

2072
01:24:36,119 --> 01:24:38,119
You know, I... I put a crimp in my evening.

2073
01:24:40,119 --> 01:24:42,119
So you want to get married or what?

2074
01:24:44,119 --> 01:24:47,119
No. We're friends.

2075
01:24:47,119 --> 01:24:49,119
I want to remain friends.

2076
01:24:49,119 --> 01:24:54,119
Okay. Check, please. Can I...

2077
01:24:54,119 --> 01:24:56,119
You're mad, aren't you?

2078
01:24:56,119 --> 01:25:00,119
Yes, of course I'm mad, because you love me. I know that.

2079
01:25:00,119 --> 01:25:03,119
Albie, I can't say that that's true at this point in my life.

2080
01:25:03,119 --> 01:25:05,119
I really just can't say that that's true.

2081
01:25:05,119 --> 01:25:07,119
I mean, you know how wonderful you are.

2082
01:25:07,119 --> 01:25:10,119
I mean, you know... You're the reason that I got out of my room

2083
01:25:10,119 --> 01:25:13,119
and that I was able to sing and, you know,

2084
01:25:13,119 --> 01:25:15,119
get more in touch with my feelings and all that crap.

2085
01:25:15,119 --> 01:25:18,119
Anyway, look, I don't want... Listen, listen, listen.

2086
01:25:18,119 --> 01:25:20,619
Listen, um...

2087
01:25:20,619 --> 01:25:24,619
So what are you up to, anyway, huh?

2088
01:25:24,619 --> 01:25:27,119
The usual. You know, I'm trying to write.

2089
01:25:27,119 --> 01:25:30,619
I'm working on a play.

2090
01:25:30,619 --> 01:25:34,119
So what are you saying? That you're not coming back to New York with me?

2091
01:25:34,119 --> 01:25:37,619
No, look...

2092
01:25:37,619 --> 01:25:39,119
I gotta go.

2093
01:25:39,119 --> 01:25:42,119
What do you mean? I flew 3,000 miles to see you.

2094
01:25:42,119 --> 01:25:43,619
I'm late. Air miles, you know?

2095
01:25:43,619 --> 01:25:45,619
I mean, you know what that does to my stomach?

2096
01:25:45,619 --> 01:25:48,500
You must know it's a hectic time for Tony. The Grammys are tonight.

2097
01:25:48,760 --> 01:25:49,319
The what?

2098
01:25:49,479 --> 01:25:51,579
The Grammys. He's got a lot of records up for awards.

2099
01:25:51,979 --> 01:25:54,680
Really? They give awards for that kind of music? I thought just earplugs.

2100
01:25:54,800 --> 01:25:57,579
Just forget it, Albie, okay? Let's just forget the conversation.

2101
01:25:57,579 --> 01:26:01,180
They give awards. They do nothing but give out awards. I can't believe it.

2102
01:26:01,619 --> 01:26:04,340
Greatest, greatest fascist dictator, Adolf Hitler.

2103
01:26:15,619 --> 01:26:35,840
I know what you're going to say.

2104
01:26:35,939 --> 01:26:37,279
I'm not a great driver.

2105
01:26:37,279 --> 01:26:39,359
You know, I have some problems with...

2106
01:26:39,359 --> 01:26:40,380
Sir, your license, please.

2107
01:26:41,479 --> 01:26:43,619
Just don't get angry or anything,

2108
01:26:43,619 --> 01:26:45,979
Because I have my license here.

2109
01:26:46,199 --> 01:26:49,479
You know, it's a rented car, and I...

2110
01:26:49,479 --> 01:26:51,079
Don't give me your license.

2111
01:26:52,559 --> 01:26:54,779
Dory, just pick up the license.

2112
01:26:55,119 --> 01:26:56,760
Oh, pick up the license. You have to ask nicely,

2113
01:26:56,859 --> 01:26:58,420
because I've had an extremely rough day.

2114
01:26:58,479 --> 01:26:59,319
You know, my girlfriend...

2115
01:26:59,319 --> 01:27:01,699
Just give me the license, please.

2116
01:27:03,420 --> 01:27:06,119
Since you put it that way, it's hard for me to refuse.

2117
01:27:06,500 --> 01:27:09,039
I have a terrific problem with authority, you know.

2118
01:27:09,319 --> 01:27:11,559
It's not your fault. Don't take it personal.

2119
01:27:13,619 --> 01:27:20,840
What's wrong, fellas?

2120
01:27:21,319 --> 01:27:22,059
Keep in touch.

2121
01:27:32,399 --> 01:27:35,319
Imagine my surprise when I got your call, Max.

2122
01:27:36,140 --> 01:27:38,920
Yeah, I had the feeling that I got you at a bad moment.

2123
01:27:38,920 --> 01:27:40,859
You know, I heard high-pitched squealing.

2124
01:27:41,939 --> 01:27:42,720
Twins, Max.

2125
01:27:43,619 --> 01:27:45,619
16-year-old.

2126
01:27:47,619 --> 01:27:50,619
Can you imagine the mathematical possibilities of that?

2127
01:27:51,619 --> 01:27:54,619
You're an actor, Max. You should be doing Shakespeare in the Park.

2128
01:27:54,619 --> 01:27:57,619
Oh, I did Shakespeare in the Park, Max. I got mugged.

2129
01:27:57,619 --> 01:28:01,619
I was playing Richard II and two guys with leather jackets stole my leotard.

2130
01:28:07,619 --> 01:28:09,619
Max, are we driving through plutonium?

2131
01:28:09,619 --> 01:28:12,479
Keeps out the alpha rays, Max.

2132
01:28:13,180 --> 01:28:14,079
You don't get old.

2133
01:28:16,920 --> 01:28:18,300
You're a thinking person.

2134
01:28:18,559 --> 01:28:19,880
How can you choose this lifestyle?

2135
01:28:20,199 --> 01:28:22,559
What is so incredibly great about New York?

2136
01:28:22,840 --> 01:28:24,059
It's a dying city.

2137
01:28:24,539 --> 01:28:25,739
You read Death in Venice.

2138
01:28:26,239 --> 01:28:28,460
You didn't read Death in Venice till I gave it to you.

2139
01:28:28,680 --> 01:28:30,979
Well, you only give me books with the word death in the title.

2140
01:28:31,140 --> 01:28:32,159
It's an important issue.

2141
01:28:32,159 --> 01:28:34,840
Artie, you are totally incapable of enjoying life.

2142
01:28:35,279 --> 01:28:36,239
You're like New York.

2143
01:28:36,720 --> 01:28:37,420
You're an island.

2144
01:28:38,140 --> 01:28:38,500
Okay.

2145
01:28:39,140 --> 01:28:41,560
If that's all that we've been through together means to you,

2146
01:28:41,880 --> 01:28:44,720
I guess it's better if we just said goodbye, once and for all.

2147
01:28:45,600 --> 01:28:46,199
You know what's funny?

2148
01:28:46,659 --> 01:28:49,020
After all the serious talks and passionate moments,

2149
01:28:49,579 --> 01:28:53,000
that it ends here, in a health food restaurant on Sunset Boulevard.

2150
01:28:54,039 --> 01:28:54,619
Goodbye, Sally.

2151
01:28:56,560 --> 01:28:57,000
Wait.

2152
01:28:58,220 --> 01:28:59,680
I'm gonna go with you.

2153
01:29:00,859 --> 01:29:01,960
I love you.

2154
01:29:01,960 --> 01:29:08,300
What do you want? It was my first play.

2155
01:29:09,300 --> 01:29:12,340
You know how you're always trying to get things to come out perfect in art

2156
01:29:12,340 --> 01:29:14,659
because it's real difficult in life.

2157
01:29:15,939 --> 01:29:19,720
Interestingly, however, I did run into Annie again.

2158
01:29:20,220 --> 01:29:22,319
It was on the Upper West Side of Manhattan.

2159
01:29:22,819 --> 01:29:24,140
She had moved back to New York.

2160
01:29:24,220 --> 01:29:25,739
She was living in Soho with some guy.

2161
01:29:26,359 --> 01:29:28,220
And when I met her, she was, of all things,

2162
01:29:28,300 --> 01:29:30,000
dragging him in to see The Sorrow and the Pity,

2163
01:29:30,000 --> 01:29:32,119
which I counted as a personal triumph.

2164
01:29:32,619 --> 01:29:35,619
And Annie and I, we had lunch sometime after that

2165
01:29:35,619 --> 01:29:38,960
and just kicked around old times.

2166
01:29:38,960 --> 01:29:49,119
Just to have my arms around you

2167
01:29:49,119 --> 01:29:54,800
Still the thrill

2168
01:29:54,800 --> 01:30:14,960
That it was the day I found you seems like old times.

2169
01:30:14,960 --> 01:30:20,899
Dinner dates and flowers

2170
01:30:20,899 --> 01:30:26,380
Oh, Tom

2171
01:30:26,380 --> 01:30:30,239
After that, it got pretty late, and we both had to go,

2172
01:30:30,340 --> 01:30:32,100
but it was great seeing Annie again.

2173
01:30:32,100 --> 01:30:34,640
I realized what a terrific person she was

2174
01:30:34,640 --> 01:30:37,500
and how much fun it was just knowing her.

2175
01:30:38,300 --> 01:30:41,359
And I thought of that old joke, you know,

2176
01:30:41,460 --> 01:30:44,319
this guy goes to a psychiatrist and says,

2177
01:30:44,319 --> 01:30:46,380
Doc, my brother's crazy.

2178
01:30:46,939 --> 01:30:47,840
He thinks he's a chicken.

2179
01:30:48,739 --> 01:30:51,679
And the doctor says, well, why don't you turn him in?

2180
01:30:51,819 --> 01:30:54,139
And the guy says, I would, but I need the eggs.

2181
01:30:55,139 --> 01:30:58,939
Well, I guess that's pretty much now how I feel about relationships.

2182
01:30:59,739 --> 01:31:03,759
You know, they're totally irrational and crazy and absurd.

2183
01:31:03,759 --> 01:31:10,659
But I guess we keep going through it because most of us need the eggs.

2184
01:31:14,319 --> 01:31:19,319
Oh, oh, oh.

2185
01:31:44,319 --> 01:32:14,299
Thank you.

2186
01:32:14,319 --> 01:32:14,939
you

2187
01:32:44,319 --> 01:32:44,939
you

2188
01:33:14,319 --> 01:33:16,319
You

